request:
compact up to revision 3, after two writes have happened

POST /v3/kv/compaction
{
  "revision": "3"
}

response:
a bare header: compaction answers when it happened, not what it removed

HTTP 200 OK
{
  "header": {
    "cluster_id": "16032618686655537237",
    "member_id": "4484589075580338506",
    "raft_term": "2",
    "revision": "3"
  }
}

request:
a point read as of revision 2, which compaction has just dropped

POST /v3/kv/range
{
  "key": "aGlzdA==",
  "revision": "2"
}

response:
HTTP 400 and code 11, `mvcc: required revision has been compacted`

HTTP 400 Bad Request
{
  "code": 11,
  "message": "etcdserver: mvcc: required revision has been compacted"
}
